Z||000000||87FieroGT||05-13-99||06:27 PM||||Recently I started to have a very strange problem. I hope someone can help me out. Whenever I start up the car for the first time in any given day it runs perfect. However, after the car has warmed up and I stop somewhere and then start the car back up the CHECK ENGINE light comes on. The car idles a lttle on the low side at this point, but the real problem is that if I rev the engine and it hits 3000 RPM the whole engine shuts down. I can then turn the car back on with no problem except the 3000 RPM problem. It will drive fine in this situation as long as I don't go over 3000 RPM. If someone could help please E-Mail me. Thanks. 
Z||000001||theogre||05-13-99||06:50 PM||||there are a couple things that could cause this.....<p>1. the tach filter. a small tin can in one of the wires from the distributor.<p>2. the ignition module<p>3. the ECM<p>the tach won't work w/o the filter, but the car will run. disconect the filter and see it the problem goes away.<p>replace the ignition module on the distributor.<p>hook up a scanner and monitor the ECM to test it.
Z||000002||theogre||05-13-99||06:51 PM||||a problem with the distributor mechanicals could also cause it.
Z||000003||theogre||05-14-99||06:16 PM||||the tach filter is a small tin can, i'm told it's usually by the coil. I don't know... I have a DIS motor.
